{"title":"1999 OIM Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer greater than 10 such that each of its digits belongs to the set {1, 3, 7, 9}. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has a prime factor greater than or equal to 11.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose, for the sake of contradiction, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has only prime factors less than 11. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be30bf51cc05760692c7ef6afeb031912331acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3,5,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />. Since there are no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa21a3234f493a4c299d7f2fdfcaa680823c1f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> nor even digits in the set of possible digits, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c3118eef3559560fcb9a32ad1ea33cc61b2e74df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, thus we must construct a number with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f416f6d21f4762339fc44616e70e0399e9f371f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />. By intuition, (see this math exchange post for proof, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/13890/in-every-power-of-3-the-tens-digit-is-an-even-number%7Cproof\">[1]</a>) every number in the form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c1937352d5a2ce7d59844f6d424d360b867a6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^n, n \\geq 3\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" />\nhas an even digit. We can also see this for powers of 7 greater than 10. Thus, this supposed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> that only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as prime factors, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d8882e2f7470b48afeb4bf819c432c74d3255c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=3^n7^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. We must now prove that any number in this form has at least one even digit when greater than 10. To prove this, notice that the tens digit is always even. Thus, such a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> cannot exist if it only has the digits in the set. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> always has a prime factor greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_OIM_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe14.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe14.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017054430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2925/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26124:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017054430 and revision id 289568. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}